{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T11:11:21.607Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"ci","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Reproduced lookup defect in PR #92\n\nTested commit: [0d30ec217955a12155038726a757bc8c441c2713](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/92). This finding concerns the proposed admission path, not a claim that the released package has this new refusal.\n\nThe mandatory lookup in [decision-admission.ts:89–96](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/0d30ec217955a12155038726a757bc8c441c2713/decision-admission.ts#L89-L96) accepts only exact equality between the configured model reference and an inventory name. Native Ollama also accepts an omitted default tag and fully qualified references to the same model. A supported installed model can therefore be rejected as `unsupported_model` before metadata inspection or inference.\n\n### Expected and actual\n\nThe goal is to resolve an installed supported model and pin inference to its immutable digest. Model-name spelling should not prevent equivalent native references from resolving, and any correction must retain digest-addressed inspection/inference.\n\nWith an inventory entry named `custom-tev1:latest`, configuration `PM_JEV_MODEL=custom-tev1` is rejected by the new lookup. Similarly, `registry.ollama.ai/library/tev1:4b` does not match the inventory spelling `tev1:4b`. Exact-tag configuration succeeds.\n\n### Sanitized reproduction\n\nThe isolated test evaluates the exact changed lookup expression with:\n\n```js\nconst models = [\n  { name: \"custom-tev1:latest\", digest: \"a\".repeat(64) },\n  { name: \"tev1:4b\", digest: \"b\".repeat(64) },\n];\n// Run the source lookup with each config.model:\n\"custom-tev1\"                            // actual: undefined\n\"registry.ollama.ai/library/tev1:4b\"      // actual: undefined\n\"custom-tev1:latest\"                     // actual: \"a\".repeat(64)\n```\n\nNative naming semantics were checked in [Ollama name parsing](https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/types/model/name.go), which supplies the default `latest` tag, and [request model resolution](https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/server/model_resolver.go). Those upstream references were inspected on current main.\n\n### Impact and limits\n\nValid configured aliases stop working for an otherwise supported installed profile. The lookup failure is reproduced with an isolated source-excerpt test. No Ollama request, provider inference, dependency installation, or full integration test was performed; metadata/tokenizer validity is a precondition, not established by this synthetic inventory.\n\n### Regression criteria\n\n- An omitted default tag, exact tagged name and equivalent fully qualified name resolve to the same installed digest.\n- Unknown references still refuse before inference.\n- Equivalent-name handling is unambiguous and follows native naming rules.\n- Model inspection and inference remain pinned to that digest; do not replace the refusal with mutable-alias inference.\n- Cover canonical-name variants in admission tests, including the exact-tag control.\n\n### Scope and deduplication\n\nThe source goal is tracked by [pm-jev-tokenizer-admission](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/0d30ec217955a12155038726a757bc8c441c2713/.agents/pm/features/pm-jev-tokenizer-admission.toon). Before filing, the review screened all 92 all-status issue/PR titles, all four ordinary issue bodies, all 49 canonical PM records at this commit, the fresh #92 discussion and related #47 discussion. No existing issue or canonical defect record covered this mechanism. Historical PR conversations were not exhaustively audited. The candidate head was rechecked unchanged immediately before filing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jev-github-21e139da0658-93"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"PR #92 admission rejects equivalent native Ollama model references"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #93: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/issues/93 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-05T05:30:53Z · updated 2026-11-05T05:30:53Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-jev#93","github_author:unbraind"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-05T11:11:21.607Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T11:11:21.607Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pm-github"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"e69cad5363d8a0491c1ae35bb98cd1df95c3e3ba3cc427b09d789f2a545a6977","item_hash_version":3,"message":"bulk-item-transaction github-import-8be387f5222f396a 8-create-pm-jev-github-21e139da0658-93-dc96e3d6ce90 apply","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7445d8aec8d527bfc8b661d0c9d1a40b6e616c5addf42ce1e8a16f32c6c69371"}
